---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
import ClassRef from '../../components/ClassRef.astro';
import Related from '../../components/Related.astro';
import ApiTable from '../../components/ApiTable.astro';
import DsaScore from '../../components/DsaScore.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const toastMarkup =`<!-- Region ships in your layout ONCE, before any toast exists,
     so injected toasts are announced: -->
<div class="bo-toast-region" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>

<!-- Server/HTMX/JS injects: -->
<div class="bo-alert bo-alert--success bo-toast">
  <div><span class="bo-alert__title">Saved.</span> PO-88213 was approved.</div>
  <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--ghost bo-btn--icon bo-alert__dismiss"
          aria-label="Dismiss">✕</button>
</div>`;
---
<Gallery title="Alerts & toasts">
  <p class="demo-note">
    Inline alerts announce only what <em>arrives</em>: add
    <code>role="alert"</code> (errors) or <code>role="status"</code> when the
    alert is inserted after load, and <a href={base + '/concepts/accessibility#live-regions'}>no
    role at all</a> when it is already in the HTML the browser parsed.
    Toasts are alerts injected into a persistent <code>aria-live</code> region — the
    region must exist before the first toast, or nothing is announced.
    <strong>Without the JS:</strong> everything above still works — the role,
    the live region and the styling are all markup. <code>initAlerts()</code>
    adds <em>dismissal only</em>, so the one thing you lose is the ✕ button;
    injecting toasts was always your code.
    <strong>Not for a field that failed validation</strong> — an error about
    one input belongs beside that input, as
    <a href={base + '/components/form'}>the form field's own message</a>,
    where it is programmatically tied to the control by
    <code>aria-describedby</code>; an alert floated above the form makes the
    reader hunt for which field it means. Use an alert for what happened to
    the <em>request</em> ("Save failed, nothing was changed"), and
    <a href={base + '/patterns/validation-summary'}>the validation summary</a>
    when several fields failed at once and the reader needs a route to each.
  </p>
  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Inline alerts</h2>
    {/* No live-region role on any of these four: this gallery shows what the
        severities LOOK like, and they are all present at load. The announcing
        case is demonstrated live by the toast section below, where the alert
        is genuinely injected. */}
    <div class="bo-alert">
      <div><span class="bo-alert__title">Heads up.</span> Approvals sync runs at 18:00.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="bo-alert bo-alert--success">
      <div><span class="bo-alert__title">Saved.</span> All changes stored.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="bo-alert bo-alert--warning">
      <div><span class="bo-alert__title">Budget at 92%.</span> CC-4021 nears its limit.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="bo-alert bo-alert--danger">
      <div><span class="bo-alert__title">Posting failed.</span> Period 2026-07 is closed.
        <a href="#">Open period settings</a></div>
      <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--ghost bo-btn--icon bo-alert__dismiss" aria-label="Dismiss">✕</button>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">The most-copied real variant after plain text: an
    alert whose body carries the way out — a link or retry, in the text where a
    screen reader meets it.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Dismissible — the button is the whole API</h2>
    <p>The page said "dismiss buttons work via <code>initAlerts()</code>" and showed
    none. Here is one, live: click the × and this alert is removed from the DOM.</p>
    <div class="bo-alert bo-alert--warning">
      <strong class="bo-alert__title">Rate card expires in 3 days</strong>
      Renew it before the next billing run.
      <button class="bo-alert__dismiss" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss">×</button>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Any <code>.bo-alert__dismiss</code> inside a
    <code>.bo-alert</code> removes it — no id, no wiring, no per-alert init. The
    behaviour is document-delegated, which is why a toast injected a minute from now is
    covered too.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Toast recipe</h2>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Toasts are ephemeral, so the sample is a trigger, not a
    static block — click it to see the real thing render, dismiss, and go away.</p>
    <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--secondary" type="button" id="toast-demo-trigger">Show toast</button>
    <div class="bo-toast-region" id="toast-demo-region" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
    <pre><code>{toastMarkup}</code></pre>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Dismiss buttons work via <code>initAlerts()</code>
    (document delegation — injected toasts covered automatically). If you auto-dismiss,
    keep toasts visible ≥ 5s and pause the timer on hover/focus (WCAG 2.2.1). Toasts do
    <strong>not</strong> float above an open modal dialog (the dialog owns the top
    layer) — render confirmations inside the dialog instead.</p>
  </section>
  <script>
    import { initAlerts } from '@busy-office/ui/js';
    initAlerts();
    document.getElementById('toast-demo-trigger')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const region = document.getElementById('toast-demo-region')!;
      // Two toasts per click so stacking order and spacing are visible —
      // ERP reality is bursts (a save + a follow-on warning), not singles.
      region.insertAdjacentHTML(
        'beforeend',
        `<div class="bo-alert bo-alert--success bo-toast">
          <div><span class="bo-alert__title">Saved.</span> PO-88213 was approved.</div>
          <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--ghost bo-btn--icon bo-alert__dismiss" aria-label="Dismiss">✕</button>
        </div>
        <div class="bo-alert bo-alert--warning bo-toast">
          <div><span class="bo-alert__title">Budget at 92%.</span> CC-4021 nears its limit.</div>
          <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--ghost bo-btn--icon bo-alert__dismiss" aria-label="Dismiss">✕</button>
        </div>`,
      );
    });
  </script>
  <ClassRef component="alert" />
  <ApiTable component="alert"
    js="Optional: initAlerts() — dismiss buttons remove their alert/toast (delegation covers injected toasts)."
    notes={[`Arrival decides the role, not severity — the <a href="${base}/concepts/accessibility#live-regions">live-region rule</a> is stated once there; short form: none at load, <code>role="alert"</code>/<code>role="status"</code> only when inserted after load.`,
            'The toast region must exist (with <code>aria-live</code>) BEFORE the first toast is injected.',
            'Toasts do not float above an open modal dialog (top layer).']} />
  <DsaScore component="alert" />
  <Related links={[["/concepts/js-behaviors", "JS behaviors"], ["/getting-started/htmx", "Using with HTMX"]]} />
</Gallery>
